    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act of 1976 added the terms Socialist, Secular, and Integrity to the Preamble.",
        "Article 32 provides the right to constitutional remedies and was referred to as the heart and soul of the Constitution by Dr. B.R. Ambedkar.",
        "Right to Property was removed from the list of Fundamental Rights by the 44th Amendment Act, 1978 and made a legal right under Article 300A.",
        "Fundamental Duties were added to Part IV-A on the recommendation of the Swaran Singh Committee via the 42nd Amendment."
      ],
      "id": "ccfoi0o"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinguish carefully between changes made by the 42nd Amendment (1976) and 44th Amendment (1978).",
        "Remember that Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) are non-justiciable, unlike Fundamental Rights.",
        "Match-the-following questions frequently test borrowed features of the Constitution (e.g., DPSP from Ireland, Fundamental Rights from USA)."
      ],
